<title>SOUTH KOREA: EZ Tech details five bln won bond issue.</title>
<headline>EZ Tech details five bln won bond issue.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The five billion won bond being issued by South Korea's EZ Tech Co Ltd exclusively for foreign investors will carry a coupon of 11.5 percent, a Securities Supervisory Board said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The non-guaranteed bond will yield 12.11 percent, it said.</p>
<p>A board official said Malaysian investors had agreed to underwrite the bonds. No further details were given.</p>
<p>Payment is by April 15.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5647</p>
</text>
